  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 18 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (will NOT be sold prior)\r\n\r\nCommanding views from the city skyline across to Devonport, this 368sqm (approx.) four-bedroom residence on a 600sqm (approx.) section presents an exceptional opportunity in the heart of St Heliers. Designed with entertaining at its core, it combines relaxed coastal living with the comfort, flow and lifestyle appeal of a truly considered family home.\r\n\r\nThe main living level is anchored by high ceilings and a gas fire, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere through every season. Two decks, positioned on opposite aspects, allow you to follow the sun and the outlook throughout the day, making the most of the sweeping city-to-Devonport views.\r\n\r\nThe lower level is devoted to leisure. A dedicated billiard room, spa and bathroom sit alongside an indoor/outdoor cooking area, while cedar bi-fold doors open fully to a private terrace and pool. Indoors and out become one seamless space, ideal for long lunches, summer pool days and late-night gatherings. \r\n\r\nOutside, a lush subtropical garden is beautifully lit at night and thoughtfully designed without lawns, offering low-maintenance enjoyment all year round.\r\n\r\nPracticality is equally well considered, with three bathrooms plus a separate toilet, a double garage within a secure gated compound, and additional off-street parking for visitors.\r\n\r\nPerfectly placed within walking distance of Achilles Point lookout, St Heliers Beach and the village shops, this is a home distinguished by its views, its entertaining spaces and its easy coastal lifestyle. A rare offering for those seeking a standout residence in one of Auckland's most coveted seaside neighbourhoods.",
